+ * (letterbox: bars on the short axis); 100 = the smallest rect that COVERS it
+ * (fill: overflow cropped). Aspect is exact at both ends and everywhere
+ * between, so this can never stretch - it only trades bars for crop. That is
+ * what makes "fake widescreen" possible: render the true 4:3 frustum, then
+ * zoom until it fills a 16:9 canvas, cropping top and bottom instead of
+ * widening the field of view (which is what exposes the unauthored edges).
+ *
+ * -1 means "whatever the scaling mode implies", which reproduces the historical
+ * letterbox and fill rects exactly - so leaving it unset changes nothing. */
